=== ARM N pre-registration (stamped 2026-09-13 06:39 UTC, before launch) — lever N (deterministic plan advance, ADR-0168) on 10-rule-in-pyproject / 35B, basin-sampled
Motivation: arm M (bench/results/plan-unchanged-10-preregistration.log) FALSIFIED the text-rail hypothesis (M3): the "Plan unchanged" rail fired, was read and acknowledged, and both fired NEW runs still doom-looped (2/2, = OLD's 7/7). The dumps showed why — the 35B does the work but will not emit status:done (b3/run1: wrote utils/duration.py, edited utils/__init__.py, wrote tests/test_duration.py, 31 tests pass, fixed a test bug; then resent an all-pending plan six times, saying "The work is already done ... I just need to mark the plan steps complete", then resent unchanged again). Per M3's pre-registered response (revise as a new lever), lever N is a deterministic harness ADVANCE.
Lever N (branch lever-n-autoadvance, opt-in Settings.plan_autoadvance / env ZAKCODE_PLAN_AUTOADVANCE): on an unchanged resend (the ADR-0168 detection, on the first resend after #432) where the current step is non-terminal but the plan has been worked on (a leaf has evidence, or the current step has a recorded outcome), update_plan marks the current step done (outcome filled from the last evidence line), records "advanced", and names the next step. STICKY: Task.harness_done is set and replace_from_author keeps a harness-advanced leaf done when the model blindly resends it non-terminal, so the full-replace cannot undo the advance and each unchanged resend walks the frontier one step. Loop notes kind=plan_autoadvance.
Cells: ONE build (main #432 + lever N) in both arms; the env flag is the only difference. OFF = ZAKCODE_PLAN_AUTOADVANCE unset (the shipped default: first-resend unchanged rail, no advance) vs ON = ZAKCODE_PLAN_AUTOADVANCE=1. 35B (zds-qwen3.6-35b), temperature 0, stable prompt identity, survey ON, verify_auto OFF, --no-pin (basin sampling, rb-10849). N=9 per arm as three interleaved blocks of three: OFF b1, ON b1, OFF b2, ON b2, OFF b3, ON b3. The bench src is set once to the lever-N build and NOT swapped (both arms share it); only the env flag toggles per cell. Runner /root/zb-armn.sh; scorer /root/armn-summary.py; dumps /root/zb-dumps/N-{OFF,ON}-35B-10-b{1,2,3} (never committed); JSONs bench/results/determinism-zakcode-pinOFF-temp0-10-rule-in-pyproject.N-*.json.
Instruments per run (arm row + largest wire dump, rb-10853): pass (verify_rc==0), turns, wall, stop_reason, trace_interventions[plan_autoadvance] and [plan_unchanged]; from the dump, the longest identical-consecutive-update_plan streak (the trigger, lever-independent), the count of "Advanced step" receipts, and whether the run reached is_complete.
Trigger note (rb-10855): the advance depends on harness-attached evidence, which a pure plan-call replay cannot reconstruct, so the trigger is not fully replayable offline; the OFF arm is the in-arm trigger baseline (arm M OLD measured 7/9 doom loops on this task, though pre-first-resend). N1 governs if the trigger is absent.
Rules (applied by the letter; measured cause stated beside each):
  N1 (trigger present): identical resends (streak >= 2) occur in >= 1 OFF run. If 0 OFF runs trigger, N2/N3 are withheld and three more interleaved blocks are run before any verdict.
  N2 (wiring): every ON run whose current step was worked-on and resent unchanged fired the advance (>= 1 "Advanced step" receipt in the dump) AND the run row carries trace_interventions.plan_autoadvance >= 1 (guard-6374: the consumer reads the field). A triggered ON run with 0 advances, or a receipt with a 0 note, blocks the merge.
  N3 (PRIMARY — the advance breaks the loop): among runs that entered the resend pattern, the doom_loop rate is LOWER with the flag ON than OFF. Arm M OFF-equivalent was 7/7 (100%) doom_loop among triggered runs. Prediction: ON <= 1/ (triggered ON runs) end doom_loop; the rest reach is_complete. If ON still doom-loops among triggered runs at OFF's rate, lever N does not break the loop either — record, keep the code (it is inert unless it advances), and the next lever is the completion gate itself, not the plan tool.
  N4 (no outcome regression; confounded aggregate): ON pass >= OFF pass - 1 at N=9. NEW-OLD <= -2 -> regression: keep opt-in, do NOT default on. The +aggregate is CONFOUNDED by entry-rate basin variance (arm M's lesson: OFF and ON are unpaired --no-pin basins and the flag cannot change whether a run ENTERS the resend pattern), so N4 is read as "no regression", not as the size of the win. verify_rc is the ground truth against a FALSE-completion win: a step advanced without its work still fails verify.
  N5 (instrument control): OFF emits 0 "Advanced step" receipts and 0 plan_autoadvance notes (the flag gates the branch); ON emits 0 advances in any run with no unchanged resend.
  N6 (no harm to healthy runs, descriptive): ON runs that completed WITHOUT any advance have pass rate and turns comparable to OFF's completed runs — the flag must not perturb a run that never triggered.
Threats: the doom loop is a basin property (arm M OFF 7/9, NEW 2/9 — unpaired), so N=9 per arm may draw few triggers in either arm; N1 governs and three more blocks follow a 0-trigger OFF arm. A false advance (marking undone work done) is caught by verify (N4) and is not worse than the doom_loop it replaces (both fail). The sticky rule could keep a step done that a capable model wanted reopened; on this 35B/task that did not arise, and the flag is opt-in — a broader-model arm would test it before any default-on.

=== ARM N RESULTS (measured 2026-09-13, 06:41–07:40 UTC on zc-01 vs zakpod1; 18 runs, --no-pin) ===
Per-arm tally (verify_rc==0 = pass; triggered = the run entered the resend pattern; doom-among-trig
= doom_loop stop_reason among triggered runs):
  OFF (flag unset): n=9 pass=6 doom=3 triggered=4 doom-among-triggered=3/4 runs-with-advance=0
  ON  (flag=1):     n=9 pass=8 doom=1 triggered=1 doom-among-triggered=1/1 runs-with-advance=1
The ONE triggered ON run (N-ON-35B-10-b3 run3): the 35B resent the SAME all-pending plan 9x in a row
(identical-submission streak=9 in the largest wire dump), the harness advance fired 5x (adv=5), the
deliverable PASSED verify (verify_rc=0), yet the run still ended stop_reason=doom_loop.

Scored by the letter:
  N1 (trigger present): PASS — OFF triggered 4/9; the doom-loop trigger exists on this task.
  N2 (wiring): PASS — the one triggered ON run fired adv=5 AND its arm row carries
     trace_interventions.plan_autoadvance>=1 (guard-6374 satisfied in situ, not just in unit tests).
  N3 (PRIMARY — the advance breaks the loop): FAIL by the letter. ON doom-among-triggered = 1/1
     (100%), NOT lower than OFF's 3/4 (75%). The advance fired but did not break the loop. ROOT
     CAUSE (executed-verified, not inferred): (a) the 35B nested a PARENT "Create utils/duration.py"
     over a same-titled child leaf; replace_from_author keyed carryover by title alone, setdefault
     kept the parent, and the child leaf then inherited the parent's empty evidence + harness_done
     =False on every full-replace, so the advance never STUCK (a clean repro froze at 0/3; a
     distinct-title control walked to completion in 3 resends — the title is the only difference).
     (b) the doom-loop guard keys on batch_signature(tool_calls) — the model's identical submission,
     NOT whether the harness made progress — so even a sticking advance races the exact-repeat guard
     and loses (a loop repro: OFF froze at 2/5 incomplete, ON reached 3/3 complete only after the
     guard was taught to reset on a harness advance).
  N4 (no outcome regression): PASS — ON pass 8/9 >= OFF 6/9 - 1. Read as "no regression", NOT the
     size of a win: ON drew only 1/9 triggers vs OFF 4/9, so the +2 is entry-rate basin variance
     (unpaired --no-pin), exactly arm M's confound. verify_rc is ground truth; the one ON triggered
     run PASSED verify even while doom-looping (the advance got the work verified), where all 3 OFF
     doom-loops FAILED verify.
  N5 (instrument control): PASS — OFF emitted 0 advances; ON emitted 0 advances in the 8
     non-triggering runs (the flag gates the branch).
  N6 (no harm to healthy runs): PASS — ON's 8 non-triggering runs pass 7/8 at turns 8–15,
     comparable to OFF's completed runs (the 1 ON completed-but-failed run had adv=0: the flag never
     fired, a basin miss, not the lever's doing).

VERDICT: N3 FAILS — lever N as shipped does NOT break the doom loop on the one triggered run, for two
compounding, now-fixed reasons. Per N3's pre-registered response (keep the code, revise as the next
lever) THIS PR ships both fixes: (a) carryover now keys on (title, is-parent) so a same-title
parent/child no longer collides; (b) the doom-loop guard resets its exact-repeat counter when a
harness advance made progress, so the frontier walk to completion is not killed mid-walk. Both are
executed-verified (repro + positive control + a loop-level regression test) and INERT unless the
opt-in plan_autoadvance is on (full suite 3833 passed, mypy clean). The N3 read rests on n=1 ON
trigger (starvation: ON 1/9 vs OFF 4/9), too thin to conclude the FIX breaks the loop — that is the
PAIRED arm's job (pin one workspace, toggle only the flag, OFF then ON back-to-back), pre-registered
separately.
